From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: snps-femto-v2: fix the AUTO_RESUME clear and the REFCLK select

qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask() takes (mask, value). Two calls have them the
other way round:

- The host suspend path pulses USB2_AUTO_RESUME and then "clears" it with
  mask 0, which writes the register back unchanged, so AUTO_RESUME stays
  set after the pulse.
- Init writes REFCLK_SEL_DEFAULT (2) as the mask and REFCLK_SEL_MASK (3) as
  the value: bit 1 is set but bit 0 keeps whatever it held, so the select
  is not guaranteed to be 2.

The downstream msm-5.4 driver (phy-msm-snps-hs.c) writes both with
(mask, value) = (USB2_AUTO_RESUME, 0) and (REFCLK_SEL_MASK,
REFCLK_SEL_DEFAULT). Found by GPT-6.1-Sol while reviewing the ROG5 USB -71
failure after a role switch; not known to cause it.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
@@ -193,7 +193,7 @@
 		usleep_range(500, 1000);
 		qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask(hsphy->base,
 					   USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_HS_PHY_CTRL2,
-					   0, USB2_AUTO_RESUME);
+					   USB2_AUTO_RESUME, 0);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
@@ -426,7 +426,7 @@
 					USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_HS_PHY_CTRL_COMMON1,
 					PLLBTUNE, PLLBTUNE);
 	qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask(hsphy->base, USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_REFCLK_CTRL,
-					REFCLK_SEL_DEFAULT, REFCLK_SEL_MASK);
+					REFCLK_SEL_MASK, REFCLK_SEL_DEFAULT);
 	qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask(hsphy->base,
 					USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_HS_PHY_CTRL_COMMON1,
 					VBUSVLDEXTSEL0, VBUSVLDEXTSEL0);
